 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
 
+## Board Publications
+
+Only account admins (including owners) with access to the board can publish or unpublish it.
+Being the board's creator alone does not grant this permission. Publishing does not change
+who can access or edit the board through the authenticated endpoints.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board. No request body is required.
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the board JSON, including its `public_url`. Publishing an
+already-published board preserves its existing URL.
+
+Anyone with the secret URL can view these read-only HTML pages without signing in:
+
+- `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key`
+- `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Only published cards are visible; drafts are never exposed. The built-in columns can
+also be opened using `stream`, `not_now`, or `closed` as the column ID.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board. Returns `204 No Content` on success, including when the board
+is already unpublished. Its `public_url` becomes `null` and the old public URL (including
+column and card links) returns `404 Not Found`. Republishing generates a new secret URL.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
